# Sensor Changelog: ROS 2 Launch Migration

Date: 2026-06-16
Branch: current workspace changes

## Summary

Migrated robot bring-up from shell-managed scripts to a native ROS 2 launch
package. This update makes `ros2 launch jmu_lunabotics master.launch.py` the
single supported startup path, moves launch defaults into a ROS-native config
file, removes legacy shell launchers, and fixes an AprilTag detector regression
introduced during the migration.

## New ROS 2 Package Structure

Added a ROS 2 package for the launch stack:

```text
package.xml
CMakeLists.txt
launch/master.launch.py
launch/sensors.launch.py
launch/rviz.launch.py
config/robot_defaults.yaml
```

This gives the repo a standard `ros2 launch` entry point and allows bring-up to
grow around launch files instead of shell wrappers.

## Single Bring-Up Entry Point

The supported robot startup path is now:

```bash
ros2 launch jmu_lunabotics master.launch.py
```

This launch flow now owns:

- camera driver startup
- image rectification
- AprilTag detection
- AprilTag pose and distance republishing
- optional raw image viewing
- future RViz inclusion

## Defaults Moved Into YAML

Robot bring-up defaults now live in:

```text
config/robot_defaults.yaml
```

This file now holds:

- camera enable/disable state
- camera device, name, frame, and calibration path
- image and camera info topic names
- AprilTag namespace, tag ID, family, and size
- detector tuning parameters
- visualization toggles

`master.launch.py` is now the only place that declares system defaults, and
`sensors.launch.py` consumes those values as an included launch file.

## Legacy Shell Launch Cleanup

Removed the deprecated shell launch path so there is only one supported bring-up
method.

Deleted:

```text
master_launch.sh
launch/launch_sensors.sh
launch/robot_config.sh
sensor/webcam/publish_camera.sh
sensor/webcam/publish_apriltag.sh
sensor/webcam/view_image_raw.sh
```

Also removed:

```text
changelog/cl_s1.mb
launch/__pycache__/
```

The duplicate `cl_s1.mb` file matched `docs/changelog/cl1_webcamera_1.mb` and
was no longer needed.

## AprilTag Pose Helper Updates

Updated:

```text
sensor/webcam/publish_apriltag_pose.py
```

Changes:

- moved configuration to ROS parameters
- removed shell-era environment-variable fallback behavior
- kept camera-relative pose and distance republishing behavior intact

This makes the helper consistent with a launch-driven ROS 2 system.

## AprilTag Detector Fix

After the migration, camera topics still published but `/apriltag/detections`
stopped appearing. The cause was an invalid parameter type being passed into
`apriltag_ros`:

- `detector.refine` had been passed as an integer instead of a boolean
- `detector.debug` also needed boolean handling

Fixed by updating launch parameter parsing and YAML defaults so these values are
passed with the types expected by ROS 2 Jazzy.

## Bootstrap and Documentation Updates

Updated:

```text
scripts/bootstrap_dev.sh
README.md
docs/setup.md
```

Changes:

- bootstrap now installs the ROS packages needed by the launch stack
- workspace build uses `colcon build --symlink-install`
- documentation now points users at the ROS 2 launch entry point
- changelog history entries were marked as historical where they still describe
  retired shell workflows

## Validation

The migration work was verified with:

```bash
python3 -m py_compile ...
colcon build --packages-select jmu_lunabotics --symlink-install
ros2 launch jmu_lunabotics master.launch.py --show-args
```

An additional targeted launch run was used to reproduce and then confirm the
AprilTag parameter-type fix.
